# =============================================================================
# .env.aio — runtime configuration for the all-in-one image (Dockerfile.aio).
#
# Copy to `.env.aio` and fill in real values:  cp .env.aio.example .env.aio
# `.env.aio` is gitignored — NEVER commit real secrets or internal hostnames.
#
# Only secrets, hostnames, and operator choices belong here. Every non-secret
# default (ports, backend=llmb, GB_ENVIRONMENT=standalone, the gbserver/callback
# URLs, frontend + artifact dirs) is already baked into the image.
#
# Consumed via:  docker run --env-file .env.aio ...   (or compose `env_file`).
# Note: env-file values are literal — do NOT wrap them in quotes. In particular,
# JSON-list settings must be UNQUOTED JSON. If you set auth providers, write:
#     AUTOTUNEX_AUTH_PROVIDERS=["disabled"]
# NOT '["disabled"]' — a leading quote makes pydantic's json.loads fail at start.
# Omit it entirely to use the standalone default (["disabled"]).
# =============================================================================

# --- AutoTuneX: external MySQL (shared with api-bridge) -----------------------
AUTOTUNEX_DATABASE_URL=mysql+asyncmy://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/SCHEMA
# Verified TLS to MySQL — mount the CA cert (see compose) and point here:
# AUTOTUNEX_DATABASE_SSL_CA=/certs/mysql-ca.pem
# AUTOTUNEX_DATABASE_SSL_MODE=verify
# The shared DB's schema is managed out-of-band (Alembic / stamped baseline);
# leave auto-create off against a real database:
# AUTOTUNEX_AUTO_CREATE_SCHEMA=false

# --- granite.build token ------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED: with JOB_BACKEND=llmb, AutoTuneX refuses to start unless the env var
# named by AUTOTUNEX_GB_TOKEN_ENV (default GB_TOKEN) is present. The entrypoint
# also uses GB_TOKEN + GITHUB_HOST (below) to configure git credentials at start,
# so runtime git pulls can authenticate against a private host. (The trainer is
# vendored at /opt/fm-tune and needs no clone — see the bash-trainer section
# below. The credentials reach git runs that have a HOME, such as gbserver's own;
# a bash build step gets no HOME, so they do not reach a git run inside one.)
GB_TOKEN=replace-me

# Private git host for runtime clones. Set to your GitHub Enterprise host.
# Leave unset to skip git credential setup (public clones still work).
GITHUB_HOST=github.example.com

# --- bash build trainer (fm-tune) ---------------------------------------------
# The trainer is vendored into the image at /opt/fm-tune and is the DEFAULT, so a
# standalone bash build needs no trainer clone (nor GITHUB_HOST creds for it), and
# the image defaults BACKEND=torch + FM_TUNE_EXTRA=core,mlx (lean, CPU-installable).
# To use another trainer checkout, mount it and point ROOT at its absolute local
# path (AutoTuneX refuses to start with a repo URL or a relative path):
# AUTOTUNEX_BASH_FM_TUNE_ROOT=/data/fm-tune
# For a GPU trainer, widen the extra, e.g. AUTOTUNEX_BASH_FM_TUNE_EXTRA=full,mlx.

# --- api-bridge: shares the SAME external MySQL -------------------------------
# The api-bridge now reads the same AUTOTUNEX_DATABASE_URL (and, for TLS, the same
# AUTOTUNEX_DATABASE_SSL_CA / AUTOTUNEX_DATABASE_SSL_MODE) set above — there is no
# separate api-bridge database configuration. It coerces the async driver to
# pymysql internally, so the single connection string configures both services.

# --- api-bridge: session signing (REQUIRED) -----------------------------------
# Generate: python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
SESSION_SECRET=replace-me
